::MCR_U06_L07_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L07_GuidedPractice_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FM.1
Question:
Item 3 is based on Multi-Step Measurement and Modeling. A savings account earns interest over time. Which answer gives the most mathematically reasonable decision?
{
~A. Apply a formula without defining the variable or context. #This is not the best answer. It skips a required modeling, calculation, unit, or interpretation step needed to meet the lesson standard.
=B. Use interest or payment information to support a practical decision. #Correct. This answer matches the mathematical relationship, uses the lesson concept in context, and explains why the result is reasonable.
~C. Use only one point or one value when the relationship requires comparison. #This is not the best answer. It skips a required modeling, calculation, unit, or interpretation step needed to meet the lesson standard.
~D. Report a number without explaining what it means in the situation. #This is not the best answer. It skips a required modeling, calculation, unit, or interpretation step needed to meet the lesson standard.
}

